1
00:00:00,265 --> 00:00:01,050
Go on.

2
00:00:01,050 --> 00:00:02,910
Try to tickle yourself...

3
00:00:02,910 --> 00:00:04,045
Right now.

4
00:00:04,420 --> 00:00:05,400
Nothing, right?

5
00:00:05,435 --> 00:00:07,636
But when someone ELSE does it...

6
00:00:07,636 --> 00:00:09,870
you completely fall apart.

7
00:00:09,870 --> 00:00:10,767
Why?

8
00:00:10,820 --> 00:00:12,040
Because your brain...

9
00:00:12,040 --> 00:00:14,600
is secretly predicting the future.

10
00:00:14,870 --> 00:00:16,160
Meet Pip.

11
00:00:16,160 --> 00:00:17,670
Six years old...

12
00:00:17,670 --> 00:00:19,322
and undefeated.

13
00:00:19,542 --> 00:00:20,500
So this week,

14
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:21,908
he has a plan.

15
00:00:21,990 --> 00:00:23,160
Tickle himself

16
00:00:23,160 --> 00:00:25,240
every single day...

17
00:00:25,240 --> 00:00:26,667
until he's immune.

18
00:00:26,708 --> 00:00:27,848
Day one.

19
00:00:28,508 --> 00:00:29,720
Day two.

20
00:00:30,428 --> 00:00:31,667
Day six.

21
00:00:33,870 --> 00:00:34,540
Here's the problem.

22
00:00:34,540 --> 00:00:35,757
Every time you move,

23
00:00:35,757 --> 00:00:38,634
your brain sends an order to your muscles...

24
00:00:38,634 --> 00:00:39,967
and a copy of that order

25
00:00:39,967 --> 00:00:41,327
back here,

26
00:00:41,327 --> 00:00:42,467
to the cerebellum.

27
00:00:42,497 --> 00:00:43,370
Its job?

28
00:00:43,370 --> 00:00:46,230
Predict exactly what you're about to feel.

29
00:00:46,230 --> 00:00:48,670
When the touch arrives right on schedule,

30
00:00:48,670 --> 00:00:50,370
your brain turns it down.

31
00:00:50,370 --> 00:00:51,662
Spoiler alert...

32
00:00:51,662 --> 00:00:53,100
it already knew.

33
00:00:53,129 --> 00:00:55,384
A tickle needs a surprise.

34
00:00:55,470 --> 00:00:56,750
And you...

35
00:00:56,750 --> 00:00:58,664
can't surprise yourself.

36
00:00:59,189 --> 00:01:01,033
So what if you could?

37
00:01:01,079 --> 00:01:02,070
In London,

38
00:01:02,070 --> 00:01:04,703
scientists built a tickle robot.

39
00:01:04,703 --> 00:01:05,466
You move a handle

40
00:01:05,466 --> 00:01:06,730
with one hand...

41
00:01:06,730 --> 00:01:08,081
and a robot strokes

42
00:01:08,081 --> 00:01:09,050
your other palm

43
00:01:09,050 --> 00:01:10,867
with soft foam.

44
00:01:10,900 --> 00:01:11,753
Move it yourself,

45
00:01:11,753 --> 00:01:13,905
and it's barely ticklish.

46
00:01:13,905 --> 00:01:14,612
But add a delay

47
00:01:14,612 --> 00:01:15,481
of just a fifth

48
00:01:15,481 --> 00:01:16,529
of a second...

49
00:01:16,529 --> 00:01:18,680
and the tickle comes back.

50
00:01:18,740 --> 00:01:20,150
Fool the prediction...

51
00:01:20,150 --> 00:01:22,333
and you CAN tickle yourself!

52
00:01:26,004 --> 00:01:26,990
Congratulations.

53
00:01:27,205 --> 00:01:29,970
He wanted to become untickleable...

54
00:01:30,165 --> 00:01:31,613
and he built a machine

55
00:01:31,613 --> 00:01:33,505
that tickles him.

56
00:01:33,625 --> 00:01:35,000
But the weirdest part

57
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:37,135
isn't about tickling at all.

58
00:01:37,135 --> 00:01:38,457
The same prediction

59
00:01:38,457 --> 00:01:41,040
turns down your own pushes.

60
00:01:41,040 --> 00:01:42,440
In one experiment,

61
00:01:42,440 --> 00:01:43,480
two people took turns

62
00:01:43,480 --> 00:01:45,310
pressing on each other's finger,

63
00:01:45,310 --> 00:01:47,933
trying to press back exactly as hard.

64
00:01:47,980 --> 00:01:49,650
Every single turn...

65
00:01:49,650 --> 00:01:50,495
the force went up

66
00:01:50,495 --> 00:01:52,900
by nearly forty percent.

67
00:01:52,953 --> 00:01:54,993
Which might explain every

68
00:01:54,993 --> 00:01:56,470
"he pushed me first"

69
00:01:56,470 --> 00:01:58,013
fight in history.

70
00:01:58,150 --> 00:01:59,070
And rats?

71
00:01:59,070 --> 00:02:01,301
Tickle a rat, and it chirps...

72
00:02:01,301 --> 00:02:03,840
a sound scientists compare to laughing,

73
00:02:03,840 --> 00:02:05,389
too high for us to hear.

74
00:02:05,389 --> 00:02:06,555
They even chase the hand

75
00:02:06,555 --> 00:02:07,500
for more.

76
00:02:07,540 --> 00:02:08,572
Some scientists think

77
00:02:08,572 --> 00:02:10,560
that's what tickling is for.

78
00:02:10,560 --> 00:02:11,511
Play...

79
00:02:11,511 --> 00:02:14,333
a way for two brains to bond.

80
00:02:14,390 --> 00:02:15,522
So your brain blocking

81
00:02:15,522 --> 00:02:16,790
your own tickle

82
00:02:16,790 --> 00:02:18,170
isn't a bug.

83
00:02:18,290 --> 00:02:19,298
A tickle is how

84
00:02:19,298 --> 00:02:20,990
your body knows...

85
00:02:20,990 --> 00:02:22,150
someone else

86
00:02:22,150 --> 00:02:23,467
is there.

87
00:02:26,160 --> 00:02:27,870
So he quit training.

88
00:02:28,110 --> 00:02:30,010
Some things only work...

89
00:02:30,010 --> 00:02:32,020
when someone else does them.

90
00:02:34,970 --> 00:02:36,150
Next week:

91
00:02:36,150 --> 00:02:37,395
what happens when you

92
00:02:37,395 --> 00:02:38,940
hold your breath.

93
00:02:39,030 --> 00:02:40,287
Subscribe...

94
00:02:40,290 --> 00:02:43,700
and remember to breathe out.

